# Project governance

Canonical docs: `.cursor/PROJECT_PLAYBOOK.md`, `.cursor/plans/`, `.cursor/state/`.

## Architecture

- Modular monolith only — no microservices split.
- Stack: Java 21 + Spring Boot 4.x REST API, PostgreSQL + Liquibase, Redis, React+TS storefront/admin, Flutter Android customer app.
- Both React and Flutter consume the same backend API.
- Environment-dependent URLs must be configurable (never hardcode production hosts).

## Security

- Spring Security + JWT access tokens + refresh-token lifecycle + RBAC.
- Do not weaken auth, CORS, or validation to make tests pass.
- EC2 demo may use HTTP on public IPv4 for school demo only — document risk; never claim production-secure.
- PostgreSQL and Redis stay private on EC2; expose Nginx :80; restrict SSH to admin IP.
- Never commit secrets, real `.env`, private keys, or credentials.

## Delivery integrity

- Authoritative task state lives in `.cursor/state/TASKS.md` — not chat history.
- Mark DONE only with acceptance criteria met, verification run, and evidence recorded.
- Never fabricate test counts, coverage, or deployment results.
- Never delete user work or reset Git to "clean up".
- Destructive DB/Git/EC2 ops require explicit authorization.
- Prefer small, verifiable tasks; finish and checkpoint before starting a new phase.
